arts, equipment upgrades, maintenance services, and customer training. The company sells its equipment and services to semiconductor chip manufacturers through its direct sales force. Axcelis Technologies, Inc. was founded in 1978 and is headquartered in Beverly, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Russell J. Low Ph.D. | CEO, President & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $573K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $73K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $14K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Axcelis Technologies, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $3.2B market cap on $839M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 46% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 35-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 41%.","The business throws off $107M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.98\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 22\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"