ricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 37% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 16% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 47% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 73% and a beta of 1.42, it amplifies market moves.","About $35.5M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 53% in the 2020 crash, 42% in the 2022 bear market and 97% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $75.04 (margin of safety -37%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 10%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $42.28 to $147 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Technology peers: EV/EBITDA 27.4 vs 16.6 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 59% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.4% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.3% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $132 on average, 28% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 46% clears the cost of capital of 11.5% by 35pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.19).","It runs a 41% gross margin and converts 13% of revenue into free cash flow.","ROE of 12% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.3x equity multiplier).","It spends 13.0% of revenue on R&D and 2.5% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $304.4M.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 7.9, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 4.77).","Working capital ties up about 300 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -3.0% over 3 years, 12.1% over 5 years and 10.8% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 30%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 11.4% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 21%.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (1.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 22, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (10 sales, net $2.3M sold).","It returns 3.8% a year to shareholders (3.8% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 1,465 employees, each generates about $573K of revenue, 1.5x the Technology median, and revenue has grown 7.1% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $73K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.2M (2x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $14K per employee."]},"profile":{"score":50.1,"head":"Red flag: priced 37% above its fair value of $75.04.","pros":["Composite 50, above the 39 line (gates 13/26)","ROIC 46.0% vs WACC 11.5%","FCF margin 12.8%","Revenue grew 12.1%/yr over 5y","Net cash of $304.4M"],"cons":["Trades 37% above fair value of $75.04","EV/EBITDA 27.4x vs sector 16.6x"],"flags":["Priced 37% above its fair value of $75.04"],"vc":{"base":75.04,"base_src":"dcf","bear":42.28,"bull":147.39,"alt_median":59.43,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.2628,"dispersion":0.0983,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":25.7875,"ev_ebitda":16.573,"pfcf":24.5483,"pb":3.6162,"roic":0.075,"gross_margin":0.4676,"fcf_margin":0.1214,"div_yield":0.0132}},"mc_quantiles":[27.23,36.19,42.28,46.42,51.05,55.03,59.34,63.22,67.63,72.18,76.54,81.67,88.48,93.59,100.48,109.17,119.39,132.4